the-firm-as-one-program-34 : List Word
the-firm-as-one-program-34 = unlines (cons "- **C11** Acquired systems and vendor software come in by equivalence and lifting ([P3: Transport of whole structures along equivalences (hyperactivity v31 §3–4)], [P4: Existing languages and standards as data, with adequacy proofs (hyperactivity v31 §5, §8)])." (cons "  When a firm acquires a team or a company it inherits systems built on different models of the same things, and integration takes years. An equivalence between the acquired representation and the firm's own carries operations, data and proofs across together. Vendor software, from order management to analytics, is lifted as data, and its outputs carry relations the firm checks instead of trusting." nil))
